course: dictionary
lesson: 16051
title: Vigour: energy and strength
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vigour means great strength, energy and enthusiasm. You can have vigour in your body when you run and jump, or in your mind when you feel eager to learn. «Sam came back from the swimming pool full of vigour.» Sam is full of energy after swimming, so vigour must mean energy.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Mia swept the floor with vigour, singing as she worked.» Mia is not sad or sleepy. She is working hard and happily, so with vigour means with energy and enthusiasm. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Mia swept the floor with energy, singing as she worked." It still makes sense.
explain: Vigour can also describe plants. «The young oak tree grew with vigour after the spring rain.» Here vigour means strong, healthy growth. The tree did not just grow; it grew strongly because it was healthy.
fact: Vigour means great strength, energy and enthusiasm.
fact: Vigour is a noun, and it is uncountable, so say «great vigour», not «a vigour».
fact: «With vigour» means hard and full of energy, as in «She worked with vigour».
fact: Vigour can describe healthy, strong growth of plants: «The tree grew with vigour».
fact: Exercise and playing outside can help you feel full of vigour.
exercise: «Sam came back from the swimming pool full of vigour.» What does vigour mean here? | *Great energy and strength | Feeling cold and tired | Being very quiet | Feeling sleepy after lunch
exercise: «The young oak tree grew with vigour after the spring rain.» What does vigour describe here? | The tree falling over | The tree's shadow | The tree's colour | *The tree's strong, healthy growth
exercise: «Mia swept the floor with vigour, singing as she worked.» Which clue shows that Mia was full of energy? | *Her singing as she worked | The brown broom | Her shoes were off | The dusty floor
test: The coach shouted, «Run with vigour!» What does he want? | *To run hard, with energy | To run backwards | To run slowly and carefully | To stop and sit down
test: Which of these is a good way to build vigour in your body? | *Playing outside and exercising | Eating only sweets | Watching TV without a break | Staying in bed all day
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to vigour? | *Energy | Sadness | Sleepiness | Weakness
